1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:00,921
There's a sea

2
00:00:00,921 --> 00:00:01,993
over Red Square!

3
00:00:01,993 --> 00:00:03,601
Right above the Kremlin!

4
00:00:03,710 --> 00:00:04,845
Don't believe me?

5
00:00:04,845 --> 00:00:06,047
Let's rewind time!

6
00:00:06,738 --> 00:00:07,714
Three hundred ten

7
00:00:07,714 --> 00:00:08,747
million years ago,

8
00:00:08,747 --> 00:00:09,321
a warm sea

9
00:00:09,321 --> 00:00:10,469
splashed right here.

10
00:00:10,552 --> 00:00:11,722
Its shells became

11
00:00:11,722 --> 00:00:12,548
white stone.

12
00:00:12,548 --> 00:00:13,925
They even named this

13
00:00:13,925 --> 00:00:15,163
age the Moscovian!

14
00:00:15,278 --> 00:00:16,808
Then a glacier came

15
00:00:16,808 --> 00:00:18,741
and dragged in boulders.

16
00:00:18,741 --> 00:00:19,868
One still sits

17
00:00:19,868 --> 00:00:21,157
in Kolomenskoye!

18
00:00:21,269 --> 00:00:23,526
Moscow's very first mention?

19
00:00:23,526 --> 00:00:25,138
A dinner invitation.

20
00:00:25,138 --> 00:00:26,589
One mighty dinner!

21
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:28,060
Prince Dmitry Donskoy

22
00:00:28,060 --> 00:00:29,225
builds the Kremlin

23
00:00:29,225 --> 00:00:30,326
from white stone.

24
00:00:30,326 --> 00:00:31,621
That same sea stone!

25
00:00:31,718 --> 00:00:32,764
The red Kremlin

26
00:00:32,764 --> 00:00:34,299
was built by Italians.

27
00:00:34,299 --> 00:00:35,206
Then the tsar

28
00:00:35,206 --> 00:00:35,695
had it…

29
00:00:35,695 --> 00:00:36,532
whitewashed!

30
00:00:36,653 --> 00:00:37,288
They cast

31
00:00:37,288 --> 00:00:38,206
the Tsar Bell

32
00:00:38,206 --> 00:00:39,406
two hundred tons!

33
00:00:39,406 --> 00:00:40,253
And it never

34
00:00:40,253 --> 00:00:40,959
rang once.

35
00:00:41,039 --> 00:00:42,089
Napoleon waited

36
00:00:42,089 --> 00:00:42,929
for the keys

37
00:00:42,929 --> 00:00:43,628
to Moscow.

38
00:00:43,628 --> 00:00:43,908
Nope

39
00:00:43,908 --> 00:00:44,468
the city

40
00:00:44,468 --> 00:00:45,098
was empty

41
00:00:45,098 --> 00:00:45,938
and burning.

42
00:00:46,022 --> 00:00:48,676
Mayakovskaya metro station won

43
00:00:48,676 --> 00:00:49,738
a Grand Prix

44
00:00:49,738 --> 00:00:50,800
in New York!

45
00:00:50,915 --> 00:00:52,488
Today thirteen million

46
00:00:52,488 --> 00:00:53,704
people live here.

47
00:00:53,704 --> 00:00:54,491
All walking

48
00:00:54,491 --> 00:00:55,992
on an ancient seabed!

49
00:00:56,108 --> 00:00:57,148
Where to next?

50
00:00:57,148 --> 00:00:57,966
Drop a city

51
00:00:57,966 --> 00:00:59,155
we'll rewind it!
